I stand in the fitting room.
There is a large mirror on the wall.
I put on a thick, blue jacket.
The color is nice, but it is too tight.
It is a very small jacket, so I cannot close it.
I need a large jacket for the winter.
I open the curtain and look out.
The shop assistant is standing right outside.
"Excuse me," I say.
"This jacket is too small."
"Do you have it in a large size?"
"I will just check."
"One moment," she answers.
After a short while, she comes back with a green jacket.
"Unfortunately, we do not have the blue jacket in your size," she says.
"But we have a large, green jacket."
"Try this one."
I put it on and look in the large mirror again.
It is soft and very warm.
"It is fantastic," I say with a smile.
"I will take it."
